{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/3165","id":1978037563,"node_id":"PR_kwDOGiE5WM515nU7","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/3165","diff_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/3165.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/3165.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3165","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/3165/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/3165/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3165/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/statuses/d6111b3e13ad98d9ac7143d4041b2ffa402dafe5","number":3165,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(validator): ignore content-type mismatches","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"With this PR, the validator will ignore the mismatch between the validate type like `json` and `form` and the content type of the incoming request.\r\n\r\nBefore this PR, it will throw the error if the validator validates a request that does not have a valid content type for validate type, including `json` and `form`:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nconst app = new Hono()\r\napp.post(\r\n  '/post',\r\n  validator('json', (value) => value),\r\n  (c) => {\r\n    return c.json(c.req.valid('json'))\r\n  }\r\n)\r\n\r\nconst res = await app.request('http://localhost/post', {\r\n  method: 'POST',\r\n  body: JSON.stringify({ foo: 'bar' }),\r\n  headers: {\r\n    // Does not set a content-type\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n\r\n// res.status will be 400!\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is inconvenient since it can't allow requests with no content type.\r\n\r\nAnd with this spec, it does not support multiple validators for the body:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\napp.post(\r\n  '/',\r\n  validator('json', (value) => value),\r\n  validator('form', (value) => value),\r\n  async (c) => {\r\n    const jsonData = c.req.valid('json')\r\n    const formData = c.req.valid('form')\r\n    return c.json({\r\n      json: jsonData,\r\n      form: formData,\r\n    })\r\n  }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this PR, it does not throw errors.\r\n\r\n### Is this a breaking change?\r\n\r\nI've changed the test behavior. However, the current implementation causes unintended results like https://github.com/honojs/middleware/issues/638. So, I think we can include this in a patch or minor release, not a major release.\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/honojs/middleware/issues/638\r\n\r\n### The author should do the following, if applicable\r\n\r\n- [x] Add tests\r\n- [x] Run tests\r\n- [x] `bun run format:fix && bun run lint:fix` to format the code\r\n- [x] Add [TSDoc](https://tsdoc.org/)/[JSDoc](https://jsdoc.app/about-getting-started) to document the code\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2024-07-19T13:36:11Z","updated_at":"2024-07-20T14:05:13Z","closed_at":"2024-07-20T14:05:11Z","merged_at":"2024-07-20T14:05:11Z","merge_commit_sha":"41718966819c7ca49f6ff7db0a259d752e62c6eb","assignee":null,"a